# Communications Bounded Context (frozen)

**Authority:** [communications-foundational-doctrine-v1.md](../../docs/communications/communications-foundational-doctrine-v1.md) · [communications-bounded-context-v1.md](../../docs/communications/communications-bounded-context-v1.md)

## Frozen authorities

Customer · Vehicle · Conversation · ConversationMessage · CallSession · CommunicationEvent · UnifiedOperationalTimeline · Observation

Do not introduce parallel authorities for transport-specific concepts.

## Transport

> **Twilio is infrastructure. Communications is the product.**

Voice, SMS, MMS, voicemail, and recordings are transports. Replacing Twilio touches the adapter only — not the communications model.

## Product split

| Product | Question |
| --- | --- |
| **ARKv2** | What work needs to be done? |
| **Companion: Communications** | Who needs my attention right now? |

Companion is the communications command center — inbox first. Not ARKv2 on a smaller screen. Mission: [companion-v1/MISSION.md](../../docs/companion-v1/MISSION.md) · Cursor: [ark-companion-communications.mdc](ark-companion-communications.mdc)

## PR litmus

- New authority or duplicate store? → reject
- Twilio behavior above transport adapter? → reject
- Phone-system operator vocabulary? → reject
- Collapse desktop work mode and mobile attention mode? → reject

**Workspace UI/impl constraints (binding):** [communications-workspace-rules.md](../../docs/engineering/communications-workspace-rules.md) · [ark-communications-workspace-guardrail.mdc](ark-communications-workspace-guardrail.mdc) — customer continuity (not messaging); relationship state above Conversation; identity never collapses; no channel inboxes or CRM list chrome.
